==Strategy==
The general strategy of this level is to stall Ensanglion with Boulder Cat and Metal Cat while slowly chipping it down with a liberal amount of random rushers until it dies. Everything else is more or less an afterthought, although bringing a Rich Cat is still recommended just to ease the level out slightly.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier's Behemoth Slayer, high damage, relatively high speed and, oddly, its long distance ability let it easily clear out crowds of Wild Doge, clear off some peons, and deal somewhat substantial chip damage onto Ensanglion and Cumulus.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]]: Metal Macho, despite the presence of 100 million billion random peons is still one of the best possible picks for this stage. With support from Courier to clear off peons and Boulder to fill in gaps, it is the single most effective way to stall out Ensanglion. More or less a requirement.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Stone is the only other real option to stall Ensanglion, alongside Metal Macho. Its incredible healthpool, high speed, and decently fast recharge time allow Boulder to rush into Ensanglion's attack range, bait out an attack, survive it, and then stall everything else at the front line for a few seconds. With large enough research combos, it can likely stall Ensanglion forever with proper timing, but beware of the Ariants burrowing into your backline, as they will stop any Boulders from reaching the boss.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Bullet Train's fast movement speed, Double Bounty and high damage makes it an effective option for sniping Wild Doges and getting large cash injections from Jackie Pengs, who will be your main source of money throughout the stage. Can also deal chip damage Ensanglion if timed right.
*[[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]]: Cat Chief is the most effective counter to Formicidean Ariants crawling into your backline and nuking your rushers. Its Massive Damage Vs. Zombies and Behemoth Slayer abilities let it 2-shot an Ariant at level 30, or nearly 1-shot them at level 50, with the remaining health on the Ariant being so low that a single Boulder Cat can kill it. Entirely useless against the boss, so make sure to time sending him out to avoid wasted cash.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]: Fishman Cat, especially with speed and damage talents can easily act as your main attacker against Ensanglion, dealing nearly 100,000 damage per hit against the boss at level 50, or in other terms, 1/28th of its health. It can easily get annihilated if you time it wrong, however, so be careful.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: By no means a requirement, or even really all that useful, however Can Can with its Double Money ability and high single target damage can easily take out the initial Wild Doges and Jackie Pengs in 1-2 hits, getting your economy started quickly.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Awakened Bahamut with talents sort of just demolishes everything. It can clear out entire crowds of peons, put significant damage on the Cumulus even when it's hiding behind Ensanglion, and deal anywhere from 200,000-600,000 damage to Ensanglion itself depending on how well you're able to time Breakerblast and/or the Sniper the Cat powerup.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Count Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Vampiric Yukimura]]: Lo and behold, one of the strongest anti-floating rushers in the game does extremely well against a stage that forces you to use rushers with a floating-type boss. Because of Vampire Yuki's Massive Damage against Floating and 100% chance to Survive a Lethal Blow, Yuki is '''Nearly Guaranteed''' to deal '''320,000''' damage to the boss at level 30, '''510,000''' damage at level 50, and a staggering '''605,000''' damage to Ensanglion at level 60. That's over a 5th of the bosses health, gone. Combine this with a very fast recharge of just over 50 seconds and a reasonably cheap cost of 3000¢, and you have one of the strongest counters to this stage.
*Any effective anti-floating or generalist rusher is very helpful in beating this stage, bring them if you have them.

